\qr\intbl {\b\i\cf14\fs20 Synopsis\cell\cell}\pard\intbl{\fs26\cf8 erase a polygon using rectangular regions - called by GML\cell}\pard\intbl\row\pard
\qr\intbl {\b\i\cf14\fs20 Prototype\cell\cell}\pard\intbl{\fs26\cf8 BOOL erase_polygon(void);\cell}\pard\intbl\row\pard
\qr\intbl {\b\i\cf14\fs20 Module\cell\cell}\pard\intbl{\fs26\cf8 {\uldb ERASEPLY.C}{\v ERASEPLY.C}\cell}\pard\intbl\row\pard
\qr\intbl {\b\i\cf14\fs20 Description\cell\cell}\pard\intbl{\fs26\cf8 This function is called repeatedly to collect arguments off the command
line from GMLI on the first call the three parameters "add" the
number of polygons and the increment size should be passed. On subsequent 
calls the parameters should be the X and Y co-ordinates of one point in the
polygon.  When all the points have been collected this function then
calls DoPolyErase to do the work and then it frees the memory allocated 
for the polygon points and returns FALSE.
Any failure will also return FALSE
\cell}\pard\intbl\row\pard
